6,570600],[9.41,9.49,9.2,9.22,600900],[9.21,9.41,9.1,9.39,520900]],"about":{"what":"Axon Enterprise (AXON). This chart runs from Sep 5, 2012 to Jan 15, 2013.","setup":"The stock rose about 64% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $8.45 and pulling back 19% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Nov 26, 2012 it closed at $8.54, its first close above the base high of $8.45. Volume that day was 927K shares, 2.16x the prior 10-day average of 429K. It didn't hold. By Dec 3, 2012 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $9.39.","lesson":"This is an example of a shakeout. The breakout failed by the rules, closing below the level three days running, and then the stock recovered and ran. Cutting it was still the right call when it happened. A failed breakout that fixes itself is worth watching for a re-entry, not a reason to ignore the exit."}}